# Line-ending policy.
#
# This file exists so that a machine's checkout setting cannot change what the
# repository contains.
#
# Why it is needed: the project is developed on Windows, where git's
# core.autocrlf often rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout. That turned
# database/charityevents_db.sql - which tools/export-database-dump.mjs writes
# with mixed endings - into an all-CRLF file on Windows, and
# `node tools/export-database-dump.mjs --check` then reported it as STALE on
# every machine except the one that generated it. The dump's content was
# correct; only its line endings differed, and the check compares bytes.
#
# Only the database scripts are pinned here. They are the files the project
# compares byte for byte, and pinning just them keeps this change from
# rewriting the line endings of every other file in the repository.

# The database scripts and the dump assembled from them.
database/*.sql text eol=lf
